---
components: ["AILabel", "AILabelActions"]
description: AI labels mark content and fields generated by AI, and open an explanation of how the AI produced them.
---

<script>
  import {
    AILabel,
    AILabelActions,
    Box,
    Button,
    ComboBox,
    DatePicker,
    DatePickerInput,
    Dropdown,
    NumberInput,
    Select,
    SelectItem,
    Stack,
    TextArea,
    TextInput,
    Checkbox,
    CheckboxGroup,
    Divider,
    RadioButton,
    RadioButtonGroup,
    Tag,
    Text,
    Tile,
    TooltipGroup,
    SelectableTile,
    SkeletonText,
  } from "carbon-components-svelte";
  import ArrowRight from "carbon-icons-svelte/lib/ArrowRight.svelte";
  import FolderOpen from "carbon-icons-svelte/lib/FolderOpen.svelte";
  import Folders from "carbon-icons-svelte/lib/Folders.svelte";
  import View from "carbon-icons-svelte/lib/View.svelte";
</script>

## Basic

Click the label to open the explanation. Put the explanation in the default slot.

<AILabel>
  <Stack gap={2}>
    <Text type="label-01" color="secondary">AI explained</Text>
    <p>This forecast was generated from the last 90 days of usage across your workspace.</p>
  </Stack>
</AILabel>

## Sizes

Set `size` to control the button size. The default is `"xs"`.

<Stack orientation="horizontal" gap={5}>
  {#each ["mini", "2xs", "xs", "sm", "md", "lg", "xl"] as size}
    <AILabel {size}>
      <p>Generated from the last 90 days of usage across your workspace.</p>
    </AILabel>
  {/each}
</Stack>

## Inline

Set `kind` to `"inline"` to render the label as text. Use `textLabel` to add text beside it.

<Stack orientation="horizontal" gap={5}>
  <AILabel kind="inline" size="sm">
    <p>Summarized from the incident timeline and the on-call notes.</p>
  </AILabel>
  <AILabel kind="inline" size="md" textLabel="Generated summary">
    <p>Summarized from the incident timeline and the on-call notes.</p>
  </AILabel>
  <AILabel kind="inline" size="lg" textLabel="Generated summary">
    <p>Summarized from the incident timeline and the on-call notes.</p>
  </AILabel>
</Stack>

## Actions

Add `AILabelActions` at the end of the explanation for related actions. The bar runs along the bottom edge of the explanation, and a primary button sits last.

<AILabel>
  <Stack gap={2}>
    <Text type="label-01" color="secondary">AI explained</Text>
    <p>Anomalies were flagged by comparing request latency with the same hour last week.</p>
  </Stack>
  <AILabelActions>
    <Button kind="ghost">View details</Button>
    <Button>Tune model</Button>
  </AILabelActions>
</AILabel>

### Icon buttons

Icon-only buttons sit before the primary button. Wrap them in a [TooltipGroup](/components/TooltipGroup): the first tooltip waits for the hover delay, and once it shows, the next shows right away as the pointer moves along the bar. The primary button can take an `icon` too.

<AILabel>
  <Stack gap={2}>
    <Text type="label-01" color="secondary">AI explained</Text>
    <p>Spend is projected to grow 12% next month, mostly from storage in us-east-1.</p>
  </Stack>
  <AILabelActions>
    <TooltipGroup>
      <Button kind="ghost" iconOnly icon={View} iconDescription="Show the source data" />
      <Button kind="ghost" iconOnly icon={FolderOpen} iconDescription="Open the forecast report" />
    </TooltipGroup>
    <Button icon={ArrowRight}>View forecast</Button>
  </AILabelActions>
</AILabel>

## Detailed explanation

An explanation can hold more than a sentence: a headline figure, what it measures, and the model behind it. Build it from `Text`, `Stack`, and `Divider`.

<AILabel>
  <Stack gap={6}>
    <Stack gap={2}>
      <Text type="label-01" color="secondary">AI explained</Text>
      <Text type="heading-06">84%</Text>
    </Stack>
    <Stack gap={2}>
      <Text type="heading-compact-01">Confidence score</Text>
      <Text type="body-compact-01">How closely the forecast matched actual spend over the last six months. Scores above 80% are reliable enough to set a budget from.</Text>
    </Stack>
    <Divider decorative />
    <Stack gap={2}>
      <Text type="label-01" color="secondary">Model type</Text>
      <Text type="heading-compact-01">Time-series forecasting model</Text>
    </Stack>
  </Stack>
  <AILabelActions>
    <TooltipGroup>
      <Button kind="ghost" iconOnly icon={View} iconDescription="Show the source data" />
      <Button kind="ghost" iconOnly icon={FolderOpen} iconDescription="Open the forecast report" />
      <Button kind="ghost" iconOnly icon={Folders} iconDescription="Compare past forecasts" />
    </TooltipGroup>
    <Button>View details</Button>
  </AILabelActions>
</AILabel>

## Fields

Put an AI label in the `decorator` slot of a field to mark its value as AI-generated. The field shows the AI gradient, and the label always renders at the `"mini"` size. Text inputs, text areas, number inputs, selects, dropdowns, combo boxes, multiselects, and date pickers have the slot.

<Box maxWidth={320}>
  <Stack gap={6}>
    <TextInput labelText="Incident title" value="Database failover in us-east-1">
      <AILabel slot="decorator">
        <p>Suggested from the alert that opened this incident.</p>
      </AILabel>
    </TextInput>
    <TextArea labelText="Summary" value="Primary database failed over after a storage node stopped responding.">
      <AILabel slot="decorator">
        <p>Written from the incident timeline and the database logs.</p>
      </AILabel>
    </TextArea>
    <NumberInput labelText="Replicas" value={3}>
      <AILabel slot="decorator">
        <p>Recommended from peak load over the last 30 days.</p>
      </AILabel>
    </NumberInput>
    <Select labelText="Severity" selected="sev2">
      <SelectItem value="sev1" text="Sev 1" />
      <SelectItem value="sev2" text="Sev 2" />
      <AILabel slot="decorator">
        <p>Set from the number of affected customers and the error rate.</p>
      </AILabel>
    </Select>
    <Dropdown labelText="Owning team" selectedId="db" items={[{ id: "db", text: "Database platform" }, { id: "net", text: "Networking" }]}>
      <AILabel slot="decorator">
        <p>Matched to the team that owns the failed service.</p>
      </AILabel>
    </Dropdown>
    <ComboBox labelText="Region" selectedId="us-east-1" items={[{ id: "us-east-1", text: "US East (N. Virginia)" }, { id: "eu-west-1", text: "EU West (Ireland)" }]}>
      <AILabel slot="decorator">
        <p>Detected from the host that sent the first alert.</p>
      </AILabel>
    </ComboBox>
    <DatePicker datePickerType="single">
      <DatePickerInput labelText="Follow-up date" placeholder="mm/dd/yyyy">
        <AILabel slot="decorator">
          <p>Scheduled two business days after the incident closes.</p>
        </AILabel>
      </DatePickerInput>
    </DatePicker>
  </Stack>
</Box>

## Selection controls

Checkboxes, radio buttons, and their groups have a `decorator` slot too. The label follows the label text or the legend.

<Stack gap={5}>
  <Checkbox labelText="Enable automatic failover" checked>
    <AILabel slot="decorator">
      <p>Recommended because this database had two outages last quarter.</p>
    </AILabel>
  </Checkbox>
  <RadioButtonGroup legendText="Billing cycle" selected="annual">
    <AILabel slot="decorator">
      <p>Annual billing costs less for usage that has been steady all year.</p>
    </AILabel>
    <RadioButton labelText="Monthly" value="monthly" />
    <RadioButton labelText="Annual" value="annual" />
  </RadioButtonGroup>
</Stack>

## Tags

In a tag, the label renders as inline text in the tag's color.

<Stack orientation="horizontal" gap={3}>
  <Tag type="blue">Forecast<AILabel slot="decorator"><p>Generated from the last 90 days of usage.</p></AILabel></Tag>
  <Tag type="green" filter>us-east-1<AILabel slot="decorator"><p>Suggested because most of the alerts came from this region.</p></AILabel></Tag>
</Stack>

## Tiles

Tiles, clickable tiles, selectable tiles, radio tiles, and expandable tiles show the AI surface and put the label in the top-right corner. On interactive tiles, the label sits outside the link, button, or label element.

<Stack orientation="horizontal" gap={5}>
  <Box width="16rem">
    <Tile>
      <h4>Usage forecast</h4>
      <p>Spend is projected to grow 12% next month.</p>
      <AILabel slot="decorator">
        <p>Projected from the last six months of spend.</p>
      </AILabel>
    </Tile>
  </Box>
  <Box width="16rem">
    <SelectableTile>
      Recommended plan: Team
      <AILabel slot="decorator">
        <p>Recommended for a workspace with 8 to 20 active members.</p>
      </AILabel>
    </SelectableTile>
  </Box>
</Stack>

## Loading

While AI generates content, show an AI skeleton in its place. Set `ai` on [SkeletonText](/components/SkeletonText#ai), [SkeletonPlaceholder](/components/SkeletonPlaceholder#ai), or [SkeletonIcon](/components/SkeletonIcon#ai).

<Box width="16rem">
  <Tile>
    <Stack gap={4}>
      <h4>Usage forecast</h4>
      <SkeletonText ai paragraph lines={2} noMargin />
    </Stack>
    <AILabel slot="decorator">
      <p>Projecting from the last six months of spend.</p>
    </AILabel>
  </Tile>
</Box>

## Data tables

A data table has three slots: `decorator` beside the title, `headerDecorator` for AI columns, and `rowDecorator` for AI rows. The cells of an AI column take the AI gradient, as the cells of an AI row do. See [DataTable](/components/DataTable#ai-label).

<FileSource src="/framed/DataTable/DataTableAILabel" />

## Modals

`Modal` and `ComposedModal` show the AI surface and put the label beside the close button. See [Modal](/components/Modal#ai-label).

<FileSource src="/framed/Modal/ModalAILabel" />

## Revert

Set `revertActive` to `true` after the user edits an AI-generated value. The label turns into a revert button. Clicking it sets `revertActive` back to `false` and dispatches `revert`, so you can restore the AI value.

<FileSource src="/framed/AILabel/AILabelRevert" />

## Direction and alignment

Set `direction` (`"top"`, `"right"`, `"bottom"`, `"left"`) and `align` (`"start"`, `"center"`, `"end"`) to place the explanation. Inside a field, the explanation aligns to the end of the label by default; elsewhere it aligns to the start. The caret always points at the label.

### Directions

<Stack orientation="horizontal" gap={10}>
  <AILabel kind="inline" size="md" textLabel="Top" direction="top">
    <p>Opens above the label.</p>
  </AILabel>
  <AILabel kind="inline" size="md" textLabel="Right" direction="right">
    <p>Opens to the right of the label.</p>
  </AILabel>
  <AILabel kind="inline" size="md" textLabel="Bottom" direction="bottom">
    <p>Opens below the label.</p>
  </AILabel>
  <AILabel kind="inline" size="md" textLabel="Left" direction="left">
    <p>Opens to the left of the label.</p>
  </AILabel>
</Stack>

### Alignment

`align` places the explanation along the side it opens on. Below or above the label, `"start"` lines it up on the left and `"end"` on the right. To the left or right, `"start"` lines it up at the top and `"end"` at the bottom.

<Stack gap={7}>
  <Stack orientation="horizontal" gap={10}>
    <AILabel kind="inline" size="md" textLabel="Bottom start" align="start">
      <p>Opens below, lined up with the label's left side.</p>
    </AILabel>
    <AILabel kind="inline" size="md" textLabel="Bottom center" align="center">
      <p>Opens below, centered on the label.</p>
    </AILabel>
    <AILabel kind="inline" size="md" textLabel="Bottom end" align="end">
      <p>Opens below, lined up with the label's right side.</p>
    </AILabel>
  </Stack>
  <Stack orientation="horizontal" gap={10}>
    <AILabel kind="inline" size="md" textLabel="Right start" direction="right" align="start">
      <p>Opens to the right, lined up with the label's top.</p>
    </AILabel>
    <AILabel kind="inline" size="md" textLabel="Right center" direction="right" align="center">
      <p>Opens to the right, centered on the label.</p>
    </AILabel>
    <AILabel kind="inline" size="md" textLabel="Right end" direction="right" align="end">
      <p>Opens to the right, lined up with the label's bottom.</p>
    </AILabel>
  </Stack>
</Stack>

### Not enough room

If a start- or end-aligned explanation would run past its container, such as a table's scroll area, it opens toward the other side. This label is aligned to the start at the right edge of a scroll box, so it opens to the left.

<Box display="flex" justify="end" overflowX="auto" maxWidth="24rem" padding={5} paddingBottom="12rem" border="subtle">
  <AILabel align="start">
    <p>Aligned to the start, but there is no room on the right, so it opens to the left.</p>
  </AILabel>
</Box>

## Portal

Set `portalTooltip` to `true` to render the explanation in a portal, so a container with `overflow: hidden` cannot clip it. Inside a `Modal`, the explanation is portalled by default.

<Box overflow="hidden" padding={5} border="subtle">
  <AILabel portalTooltip>
    <p>Generated from your last three billing cycles.</p>
  </AILabel>
</Box>

## Server rendering

A filled `decorator` slot renders the AI surface on the server, so the surface does not pop in after the page loads. The server can't tell what the slot holds. If it holds another element, or a label with `revertActive` set, the surface drops once the page loads. Data table rows and `headerDecorator` columns can each differ, so their gradient appears once the page loads.
